summary:
  relayPlaybackFell rebuilds the tap on any player error against the relay
  source, including one that arrives after a park has already stopped the
  player — and the rebuild's UP ack plays the room awake.

history:
  A park stops the player but leaves the source pointing at the loopback tap
  and the engine armed. When the tap's own ffmpeg then falls over, Qt raises an
  error against that stopped source; the road guarded only on `relay` and
  `active`, both still true, so it re-armed and the UP ack played. The same
  terminus as the window-cap re-arm, reached by a second door. Found 2026-09-14
  while hunting issue #13, "randomly starts playing on its own".

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftEngine.qml

find:
          if (app._tsPaused) return false;

replace:
          if (false) return false;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_timeshiftengine.qml::test_a_parked_relay_is_not_rebuilt_by_a_late_player_error.
  Line-neutral.
